1
00:00:32,899 --> 00:00:34,579
Dear listeners and friends,

2
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,640
today is New Year's Eve on the lunar calendar,

3
00:00:36,939 --> 00:00:39,060
and we are about to step into a new year.

4
00:00:39,259 --> 00:00:40,740
At this festive moment,

5
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,420
on behalf of all the staff at our station,

6
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:45,280
to all industries across the nation,

7
00:00:45,659 --> 00:00:47,380
and comrades on every front,

8
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,960
to compatriots in Taiwan, China, Hong Kong, Macao, and abroad,

9
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:52,700
and to all ethnic groups nationwide,

10
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,500
I extend our warmest holiday greetings.

11
00:00:55,759 --> 00:00:57,579
Wishing you all a joyful life

12
00:00:57,679 --> 00:00:59,119
and a Happy New Year!

13
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:01,380
Dear friends,

14
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:05,680
the holidays are a time for family reunions,

15
00:01:05,859 --> 00:01:07,500
but at this very moment,

16
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:08,959
many comrades

17
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:11,859
are still standing fast at their posts.

18
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:18,219
You're back!

19
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:19,599
Come on, hurry in!

20
00:01:20,959 --> 00:01:23,180
Did you make all this?

21
00:01:24,319 --> 00:01:26,159
Not bad, huh? It really feels like New Year's!

22
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:27,239
Come on, the food's ready.

23
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,219
It's all piping hot.

24
00:01:29,659 --> 00:01:30,980
Come take a look.

25
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,000
My dad's specialty dish:

26
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:34,980
pork belly with pickled cabbage.

27
00:01:35,239 --> 00:01:35,980
Smells incredible.

28
00:01:36,439 --> 00:01:37,540
Smells to die for!

29
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:39,480
Right?

30
00:01:39,959 --> 00:01:40,659
And for you,

31
00:01:40,859 --> 00:01:42,060
I also prepared a gift.

32
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:43,900
Check it out.

33
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:44,519
What is it?

34
00:01:51,159 --> 00:01:51,599
Look.

35
00:01:53,159 --> 00:01:54,680
Wh-What is this?

36
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,540
Can't you tell?

37
00:01:59,359 --> 00:02:00,400
In theory,

38
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:03,700
This is egg dumpling, this is rice cake.

39
00:02:04,219 --> 00:02:06,159
Don't you folks from Shanghai eat this?

40
00:02:06,819 --> 00:02:08,360
I'm not sure if I made them right.

41
00:02:12,199 --> 00:02:14,120
This is egg dumpling, this is rice cake?

42
00:02:15,379 --> 00:02:16,199
Let me try some.

43
00:02:17,599 --> 00:02:18,300
You made this?

44
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:29,080
How is it?

45
00:02:31,759 --> 00:02:32,620
Doesn't look like it,

46
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:36,120
but it really tastes authentic.

47
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:37,879
That's good, then.

48
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,340
You're from Shanghai, right?

49
00:02:40,659 --> 00:02:41,120
Come on, come on.

50
00:02:41,139 --> 00:02:42,000
Hurry, let's eat.

51
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:43,520
I have a gift for you, too.

52
00:02:47,699 --> 00:02:48,620
I finished knitting it.

53
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:50,699
Try it on.

54
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:51,479
Alright, let me try it on.

55
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:00,340
How is it?

56
00:03:01,159 --> 00:03:02,439
It's... it fits really well.

57
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:04,960
Are you kidding? Look at my handiwork!

58
00:03:04,979 --> 00:03:05,460
Does it look good?

59
00:03:08,159 --> 00:03:08,800
Really good.

60
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,219
Didn't you say it'd be a sweater, though?

61
00:03:12,259 --> 00:03:13,479
How come it's a vest?

62
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,500
Isn't having no sleeves...

63
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:17,879
...so it's easier for you to fight?

64
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:20,780
No, no more fighting, no more fighting.

65
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:21,879
I'm never getting into fights again.

66
00:03:22,759 --> 00:03:23,939
Come on, hurry up, let's eat.

67
00:03:30,939 --> 00:03:31,879
This is so good!

68
00:03:42,460 --> 00:03:43,740
Today is New Year's Eve.

69
00:03:44,259 --> 00:03:44,819
It's the New Year.

70
00:03:45,259 --> 00:03:46,460
We're all having a reunion dinner together,

71
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:48,560
and I'm genuinely thrilled.

72
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:49,520
Tell you what,

73
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,039
let's all toast Brother He.

74
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:51,919
Come on.

75
00:03:52,259 --> 00:03:52,560
Cheers.

76
00:03:52,699 --> 00:03:53,159
Here, Brother He.

77
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:54,319
To you, to you, to you!

78
00:03:54,379 --> 00:03:55,180
To you, Brother! Cheers.

79
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:06,460
What kind of firecrackers are those?

80
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:08,259
Sounds like gunshots.

81
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,199
I'll go check outside.

82
00:04:12,759 --> 00:04:13,180
Lao Ba.

83
00:04:13,699 --> 00:04:14,419
Sit down, sit down.

84
00:04:15,599 --> 00:04:16,899
Let's use our high spirits

85
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,420
to drown out that racket.

86
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:19,399
Problem solved, right?

87
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:20,019
Brother.

88
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:20,439
Right.

89
00:04:20,439 --> 00:04:21,819
Keep drinking, have some more.

90
00:04:22,339 --> 00:04:23,560
A few drinks, and you won't hear a thing.

91
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,459
Nothing but pure joy.

92
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,420
Come on, drink up.

93
00:04:34,839 --> 00:04:35,860
Brother, um...

94
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:37,319
I need to step out for a minute.

95
00:04:38,639 --> 00:04:39,439
It's New Year's, after all.

96
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,860
Those petty officials in charge,

97
00:04:41,439 --> 00:04:42,579
we've gotta grease their palms.

98
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:44,060
I'll be right back.

99
00:04:49,639 --> 00:04:50,800
Those two aren't leaving, right?

100
00:04:51,379 --> 00:04:52,259
Neither of them is leaving.

101
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:52,920
They'll stay here to keep you company.

102
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:53,740
I can go by myself.

103
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:54,740
Go take care of it, go on.

104
00:04:55,139 --> 00:04:55,399
All right.

105
00:04:55,459 --> 00:04:56,160
I'll head out now.

106
00:04:57,379 --> 00:04:58,540
Yan'er, come help me find something.

107
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:28,180
Don't worry.

108
00:05:30,519 --> 00:05:31,040
I'll wait for you.

109
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:41,259
Brother,

110
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:43,019
let me feed you a dumpling.

111
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,540
Brother,

112
00:05:47,699 --> 00:05:48,980
let's have a drink, just the two of us.

113
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:58,819
Happy Spring Festival!

114
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:30,759
Haizhu.

115
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:32,500
I have something to tell you.

116
00:06:34,959 --> 00:06:36,180
I have something to tell you, too.

117
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,319
Can I go first?

118
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,319
I...

119
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,579
I wanted to say...

120
00:06:57,519 --> 00:06:58,220
could the two of us,

121
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,819
after New Year's, come spring,

122
00:07:01,579 --> 00:07:03,100
take some time off?

123
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:06,740
I'll go back to Shanghai with you.

124
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,860
Could I meet your parents?

125
00:07:15,680 --> 00:07:16,399
I've actually...

126
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,639
mentioned you to them before.

127
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:23,879
If you want to go, that's fine.

128
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:27,319
What do you plan to tell them?

129
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:32,399
I want to put their minds at ease,

130
00:07:33,399 --> 00:07:34,339
and let them know...

131
00:07:34,899 --> 00:07:36,879
someone's looking after you in Songliao.

132
00:07:37,339 --> 00:07:38,060
That's nice.

133
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:40,680
And I also wanted to say...

134
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,980
I... I'll work really hard.

135
00:07:45,699 --> 00:07:46,540
I'll do my best...

136
00:07:46,939 --> 00:07:49,480
to become maintenance crew chief soon,

137
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:51,519
so the plant assigns us an apartment.

138
00:07:53,079 --> 00:07:53,620
That way,

139
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:55,199
our life together...

140
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:58,199
will have something to look forward to.

141
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:03,879
I...

142
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:06,920
Well...

143
00:08:08,579 --> 00:08:09,120
Zhou Meng,

144
00:08:10,939 --> 00:08:11,660
I want to marry you.

145
00:08:28,259 --> 00:08:29,100
Look, it's fine.

146
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:30,699
If you want to think it over, that's fine.

147
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:47,259
So, what were you going to say earlier?

148
00:08:52,399 --> 00:08:53,360
I wanted to say...

149
00:08:56,019 --> 00:08:56,860
I never thought...

150
00:08:57,860 --> 00:08:59,460
spending New Year's like this is so nice.

151
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,019
From now on,

152
00:09:09,299 --> 00:09:10,720
let's spend every New Year together.

153
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:41,519
Bro.

154
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:42,759
When we finish eating,

155
00:09:42,899 --> 00:09:43,960
let's play some mahjong together.

156
00:09:47,879 --> 00:09:48,320
Bro?

157
00:09:51,620 --> 00:09:52,340
He's asleep.

158
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:54,820
He's usually not like this.

159
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:00,960
You two stop poking him.

160
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:01,759
Let him sleep for a bit.

161
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:04,419
You bastards! Ptui!

162
00:10:08,039 --> 00:10:08,840
You two drugged him!

163
00:10:19,899 --> 00:10:20,779
Get outta here!

164
00:10:23,379 --> 00:10:24,559
I also want a dog.

165
00:10:26,139 --> 00:10:28,200
Let's call it Blackie then.

166
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:29,220
Sure.

167
00:10:29,379 --> 00:10:30,120
Any name works.

168
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:30,980
Then how about Red?

169
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:32,980
Blackie's better.

170
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:34,299
Because you're so dark.

171
00:10:35,299 --> 00:10:35,759
And...

172
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:38,320
we need the four must-have wedding items.

173
00:10:40,620 --> 00:10:42,179
Do you want a daughter or a son?

174
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:46,139
I-I've never thought about it.

175
00:10:46,399 --> 00:10:48,600
No way, you have to pick one.

176
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:51,600
Th-Then I'd want a daughter.

177
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,259
I want a son.

178
00:10:55,059 --> 00:10:56,080
Then let's have two.

179
00:10:57,539 --> 00:10:58,019
Right.

180
00:10:58,879 --> 00:11:00,779
A daughter taking after me,

181
00:11:01,259 --> 00:11:02,240
and a son taking after you.

182
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:03,000
How about that?

183
00:11:04,019 --> 00:11:05,100
A son better not take after me.

184
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:07,220
His dad's already enough of a headache,

185
00:11:07,559 --> 00:11:08,259
getting into fights every day.

186
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:09,559
A son would just make you worry too.

187
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:14,460
No...

188
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:15,440
That's not it.

189
00:11:15,539 --> 00:11:16,620
That's not what I meant.

190
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:17,940
I... I mean...

191
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,259
I already promised you.

192
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:23,700
We'll just live a steady life from now on.

193
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:24,820
And...

194
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,480
the things that make you worry,

195
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:27,419
I'll never do them again.

196
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:33,659
It's a deal?

197
00:11:34,899 --> 00:11:35,759
I... It's a deal.

198
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:42,740
You promised me.

199
00:11:43,919 --> 00:11:44,679
No backing out.

200
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:46,299
I won't back out.

201
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:47,899
I'll never go back on my promise to you.

202
00:11:58,840 --> 00:11:59,519
What's the matter with you?

203
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:01,080
Hey, don't... don't cry!

204
00:12:02,799 --> 00:12:04,059
No, I'm not backing out.

205
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:05,080
You're regretting it.

206
00:12:05,759 --> 00:12:07,279
No, I'm not.

207
00:12:08,659 --> 00:12:09,740
It's just...

208
00:12:11,179 --> 00:12:13,700
You seem really different today.

209
00:12:14,379 --> 00:12:15,559
How am I different?

210
00:12:20,659 --> 00:12:24,539
Why do you seem so dependable?

211
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:26,480
Hey, you...

212
00:12:26,679 --> 00:12:28,259
Stop wobbling!

213
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,820
If you don't rock, I won't wobble!

214
00:12:31,659 --> 00:12:34,440
From now on, let's live a good life,

215
00:12:34,580 --> 00:12:37,340
our own sweet life together, okay?

216
00:12:37,519 --> 00:12:40,879
We'll make our life truly thrive.

217
00:12:41,159 --> 00:12:42,580
No more getting mad,

218
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,279
arguing, or fighting.

219
00:12:44,679 --> 00:12:45,399
Okay?

220
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,519
Okay, okay, okay.

221
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,139
It'll definitely thrive.

222
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:50,000
Our life will definitely flourish.

223
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:51,840
Anything that makes you worry,

224
00:12:51,899 --> 00:12:52,919
I definitely won't do again.

225
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:54,539
Don't worry.

226
00:12:55,580 --> 00:12:56,679
I can't make you worry anymore.

227
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:57,799
And I won't get into fights anymore.

228
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:36,039
Ziwen.

229
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:37,139
Zhuzi.

230
00:13:37,639 --> 00:13:39,080
What brings you here on New Year's Eve?

231
00:13:39,659 --> 00:13:40,200
Come on in.

232
00:13:41,879 --> 00:13:43,480
I was passing by, thought I'd drop in.

233
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:47,320
She's asleep.

234
00:13:50,039 --> 00:13:51,039
You've got this place fixed up nice.

235
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,320
Really feels like New Year's.

236
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:53,779
It's alright.

237
00:13:55,179 --> 00:13:56,679
Well, since she's asleep,

238
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:57,879
let's head somewhere else.

239
00:13:58,039 --> 00:13:58,740
Find a spot to chat.

240
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,820
Sure, give me a second.

241
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:12,500
Zhuzi.

242
00:14:13,679 --> 00:14:14,139
What?

243
00:14:14,559 --> 00:14:15,580
Only brought one mug.

244
00:14:16,799 --> 00:14:18,399
What, grossed out by me?

245
00:14:20,519 --> 00:14:21,419
How's the dance hall?

246
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:24,340
Pretty good.

247
00:14:25,799 --> 00:14:28,200
None of that shady crap going on now.

248
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:29,159
Don't worry.

249
00:14:30,659 --> 00:14:32,000
What about your wound? All healed?

250
00:14:32,399 --> 00:14:33,259
It's been fine for ages.

251
00:14:33,399 --> 00:14:34,139
I'm tough as nails.

252
00:14:37,539 --> 00:14:40,039
That Zhang Haoran and Sun Biao business...

253
00:14:41,559 --> 00:14:42,179
...is it all settled now?

254
00:14:52,580 --> 00:14:53,139
Look...

255
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:55,820
Ziwen,

256
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:58,120
you know, I...

257
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,340
I wanted to talk to you about something.

258
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:04,879
From now on,

259
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:09,159
all that street fighting and killing,

260
00:15:10,139 --> 00:15:11,159
I'm not getting involved anymore.

261
00:15:12,559 --> 00:15:13,519
And that dance hall,

262
00:15:14,740 --> 00:15:16,220
Daguang can just manage it on his own.

263
00:15:17,399 --> 00:15:18,460
Here's what I'm thinking...

264
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:22,200
Ziwen, I don't care if you laugh at me,

265
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:26,200
but I don't have grand ambitions.

266
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:28,960
I just want to be an honest worker.

267
00:15:31,399 --> 00:15:32,679
Life in the factory,

268
00:15:33,279 --> 00:15:33,720
it's...

269
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,019
it's steady.

270
00:15:36,659 --> 00:15:37,820
It puts my mind at ease.

271
00:15:40,919 --> 00:15:41,519
Steady?

272
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:44,659
Liu Haizhu, you're not the steady type.

273
00:15:50,059 --> 00:15:50,659
Besides,

274
00:15:51,759 --> 00:15:53,519
some people, some things...

275
00:15:54,779 --> 00:15:56,240
you can't avoid them just by hiding.

276
00:15:58,139 --> 00:16:00,539
What could happen to me at the factory?

277
00:16:02,019 --> 00:16:02,940
Well, actually...

278
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:04,980
A deputy director keeps picking on me.

279
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:07,480
He's just a deputy, though.

280
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:08,580
Once the old director returns,

281
00:16:08,679 --> 00:16:09,740
his days will be numbered anyway.

282
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:12,059
Besides,

283
00:16:14,059 --> 00:16:15,460
I can always just stay out of his way.

284
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:18,000
I'll just walk away if I see him.

285
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,019
I won't butt heads with him anymore.

286
00:16:19,419 --> 00:16:19,960
What's he gonna do?

287
00:16:20,039 --> 00:16:21,320
It's not like he can... right?

288
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:22,919
Stop me from living my life.

289
00:16:25,799 --> 00:16:26,480
Hide?

290
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:28,779
Take it?

291
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:33,419
That doesn't sound like you, Liu Haizhu.

292
00:16:34,580 --> 00:16:35,539
And now,

293
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:42,899
I'm ready to settle down.

294
00:16:45,519 --> 00:16:47,179
You two getting married?

295
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:53,580
You... you're the first to know.

296
00:16:54,919 --> 00:16:56,120
That's great news, Zhuzi!

297
00:16:56,659 --> 00:16:57,279
It sure is.

298
00:16:58,639 --> 00:16:59,840
Then we've got to drink to that!

299
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:00,679
Let's drink!

300
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:13,740
Zhuzi,

301
00:17:18,119 --> 00:17:18,680
today,

302
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:20,319
I want to congratulate you.

303
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:22,059
From the bottom of my heart.

304
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:30,799
Appreciate it.

305
00:17:40,039 --> 00:17:40,500
Zhuzi,

306
00:17:42,859 --> 00:17:44,279
walk your own path steady,

307
00:17:45,519 --> 00:17:47,599
and keep your fate in your own hands.

308
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:49,019
Otherwise,

309
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:51,539
someone could take it back just like that.

310
00:17:59,519 --> 00:18:00,200
Ziwen,

311
00:18:01,839 --> 00:18:02,940
hearing you say that...

312
00:18:05,019 --> 00:18:06,500
I don't really follow.

313
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:08,000
What do you mean?

314
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:09,839
Hinting at me?

315
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:16,440
It's nothing.

316
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:17,779
You don't need to understand.

317
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:22,880
But Zhuzi, remember this.

318
00:18:24,259 --> 00:18:25,220
No matter when,

319
00:18:26,859 --> 00:18:27,859
with me, Feng Ziwen,

320
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:30,019
there will always be a seat for you.

321
00:18:34,119 --> 00:18:34,680
I'm off.

322
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:36,160
Take care.
